    'Broca’s area':'speech-production functions, typically in left frontal cortex',
    'Wernicke’s area':'language-comprehension functions, typically in left temporal cortex',
    'Orbitofrontal cortex':'anticipating consequences and regulating impulses/social decisions',
    'Primary motor cortex':'voluntary movement commands from the strip anterior to the central sulcus',
    'Primary somatosensory cortex':'body sensory processing in the strip posterior to the central sulcus',
    'Corpus callosum':'a major axonal connection between cerebral hemispheres',
    Meninges:'protective membranes surrounding CNS tissue',
    Ventricles:'cavities containing circulating cerebrospinal fluid',
    'Cerebrospinal fluid':'fluid cushioning neural tissue in and around CNS spaces',
    Dendrites:'collection of incoming information',
    Soma:'the cell body, including integration and cellular maintenance',
    Axon:'electrical output conduction toward terminals',
    'Axon terminal':'transmitter release at a communication junction',
    'Synaptic vesicle':'storage of neurotransmitter before release',
    Myelin:'axonal insulation that speeds conduction',
    'Node of Ranvier':'a gap between myelin segments where a spike is regenerated',
    'Glial cells':'support, nutrients, barrier-related functions and myelin',
    'Glial cell':'support, nutrients, barrier-related functions and myelin',
    'Synaptic cleft':'the gap between the sending terminal and the receiving cell',
    'Postsynaptic receptor':'a receiving-cell binding site translating transmitter binding into an effect',
    Autoreceptor:'a sending-cell receptor detecting its own transmitter for feedback',
    Reuptake:'transmitter transport back into the releasing neuron',
    'Enzymatic breakdown':'chemical inactivation of a transmitter',
    Diffusion:'movement of molecules away from the release site',
    'Resting potential':'the baseline voltage difference, with the interior negative relative to the exterior',
    Depolarization:'a change toward a less-negative membrane voltage',
    Hyperpolarization:'a change to a more-negative membrane voltage',
    Repolarization:'return toward negative voltage after the spike peak',
    'Refractory period':'a brief period when refiring is impossible or more difficult',
    Threshold:'the depolarization level needed to trigger a spike',
    'Firing rate':'the number of spikes emitted over time',
    'Sensory/afferent neuron':'information traveling toward the CNS',
    'Motor/efferent neuron':'commands traveling outward from the CNS',
    Interneuron:'connection and integration within CNS circuits',
    'Somatic system':'skeletal-muscle control and associated sensory pathways',
    'Autonomic system':'regulation of visceral organs and glands',
    'Enteric system':'gut neuronal networks regulating digestion and communicating with brain/endocrine systems',
    'Sympathetic branch':'organ-specific mobilization for action',
    'Parasympathetic branch':'organ-specific maintenance and recovery',
    Pineal:'melatonin and sleep–wake cycles',
    Thyroid:'thyroid hormones and metabolic-rate regulation',
    Adrenals:'stress-related hormones including cortisol',
    'Pancreatic islets':'insulin and metabolic regulation',
    'Ovaries/testes':'sex hormones under pituitary regulation',
    Pituitary:'direct hormone release and target-gland regulation under hypothalamic control',
    Oxytocin:'breastfeeding and social-bonding associations',
    Vasopressin:'fluid regulation and social-function associations',
    'Growth hormone':'growth and regeneration',
    Melatonin:'sleep–wake cycles',
    Cortisol:'stress-related signaling',
    Insulin:'metabolic regulation',
    Acetylcholine:'muscle contraction, learning, memory, attention and sleep',
    Epinephrine:'sympathetic mobilization including pupil, blood-flow and blood-sugar responses',
    Norepinephrine:'arousal, vigilance and sympathetic functions',
    Serotonin:'sleep–wake, appetite, mood and aggression-regulation functions',
    Dopamine:'movement, planning, reward and motivation',
    GABA:'major inhibitory amino-acid signaling',
    Glutamate:'major excitatory amino-acid signaling, learning and memory',
    CCK:'peptide signaling associated with digestion and satiety',
    Endorphins:'endogenous peptide signaling associated with pain reduction',
    'Substance P':'peptide signaling associated with pain, inflammation and stress',
    SSRI:'inhibition of serotonin reuptake',
    MAOI:'inhibition of enzymatic monoamine breakdown',
    'Tricyclic antidepressant':'reuptake inhibition, with norepinephrine emphasized in lecture',
    Naloxone:'opioid-receptor antagonism',
    Benzodiazepine:'enhancement of GABA receptor responses',
    Cocaine:'dopamine/norepinephrine reuptake inhibition',
    Amphetamine:'increased transmitter availability through release and transport effects',
    Nicotine:'activation of nicotinic acetylcholine receptors',
    Opioid:'activation of receptors responsive to endogenous opioid peptides',
    LSD:'serotonin-related receptor action',
    THC:'cannabinoid-receptor action, including reward and memory effects',
    Caffeine:'adenosine-receptor antagonism',
    MDMA:'strong serotonin release effects, with smaller dopamine and oxytocin effects described',
